  "A Tudor Revival library by Fisher and Lawrie, built in 1911 by P.H. Wind and Sons, with a stepped gable and keyhole windows. It was the library until 1975 and the county historical society's museum from 1977 to 1998, then stood empty after pipe damage. It was on the National Register from 2001 and was torn down in 2022. What stands on the site now was not found.",
